Kernel object lookups (ObjectTable::LookupObject) take a reader lock of the table instead of the process-wide global critical region; the table's changes take it as the writer inside the global lock. Run 46 at stock: the main thread spent ~4 % of its time queued on the global lock (2.9 thousand contended locks a second).

